# Managed by proxvex (pg_client_cert=true). Replace via the pg_hba_content parameter.
#
# Default policy: client-certificate authentication for all TCP/IP connections.
# The certificate Common Name (CN) must match the requested database user.
# Unix-socket connections stay trusted so the container's own initdb /
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD bootstrap / admin maintenance keep working.
#
# To require a password in addition to the certificate, replace this file
# (upload via the pg_hba_content parameter) with e.g.:
#   hostssl all all 0.0.0.0/0 scram-sha-256 clientcert=verify-ca
#
# TYPE   DATABASE  USER  ADDRESS     METHOD
local    all       all               trust
hostssl  all       all   0.0.0.0/0   cert
hostssl  all       all   ::/0        cert
